le food at McDonald's in order to  give everybody a meaningful raise is a  very valid and Powe  notable trade to be made so when we get  these black and white questions isn't a  $15 minimum wage bad because it'll cause  inflation the question needs to be how  much inflation will it cost and how does  that relate to the overarching cost of  living in these areas and that's where  I've read increasingly very good  economic analyses which say $15 minimum  wage is probably too low in some high  cost of living places but it may be too  high in some other places in low cost of  living parts of the country with a much  lower current minimum wage going to 15  could double the minimum wage that may  be out of line with what the local  economy needs or what the local economic  parameters dictate that's not me being  against the $15 minimum wage in some  places it should be 22 when you look at  cost of living this is me saying that  any one-size-fits-all black-white  thinking about this issue is likely to  be wrong and we have to look at all of  these issues in more detail any policy  has an upside and a downside and  economics the science of economics done  well and economic analyses can tell us  when the benefit outweighs the cost for  the broader betterment of society let me  know what you think we have a great  bonus show for you today don't miss it  become a member at join pakman.com or  become a patron at patreon.com slash  david pakman show to get instant access  to today's bonus show
 

